  "definition": "In this packet, ACC refers to the normal form of the ACACA gene, located near 17q21. It produces acetyl-CoA carboxylase 1, which helps the body make long-chain fatty acids, and changes in this gene are linked with acetyl-CoA carboxylase 1 deficiency.",
